# Nissan Micra K12 three-door hatchback, 2003-2010.
#
# The Sunderland-built K12: the rounded body with the large ovoid headlamps
# that sit almost on top of the wings, the sharply kicked-up rear window line
# and the rear glass ending above a painted lower hatch, which carries the
# number plate just above the bumper. The 2003 launch car is
# modelled; the 2005 and 2007 K12C facelifts are not represented.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nissan_Micra
#
# Dimensions 3.719 x 1.680 x 1.540 m, wheelbase 2.430 m (Wikipedia infobox).
#
# Shape reference: image 1 is a true level side elevation of a five-door car,
# used for the shell because no three-door side view exists; images 2 and 3
# are the UK three-door launch car and govern the front, the rear and the
# glasshouse. The two bodies share the front end, floorpan and wheelbase.
#
# Colours: grade (d); no UK colour list was found, although the July 2009
# Nissan GB price list records ten colours without naming them. White, Red,
# Blue and Silver are plain names. Weights 12, 10, 9, 8, total 39, provisional.
#
# Speed 160 km/h. Comfort 60/420, on the line 330 + 1.5 x 60. Classes 0,1.
# Dates: intro 15 January 2003, the UK launch date; retire 2010, when
# Sunderland built its last K12 in July and the K13 replaced it.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/nissan-micra-k12.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/nissan-micra-k12.dae. References:
# citycars/references/nissan-micra-k12/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: the rear glass ends above a painted lower hatch and the
# plate sits on that hatch just above the bumper, as the photographs show; the
# 2005 and 2007 K12C facelifts are not represented. The bumper corners, the
# glass-to-hatch join and the lamp internals are simplified.


